BorrowCapability
├── initializeBorrow
│   ├── requires a Merkle-authorized adapter self-call
│   ├── rejects invalid targets, token, minimum, query or offset atomically
│   └── fixes configuration once in the adapter's storage namespace
├── borrow
│   ├── rejects direct callers and a mismatched selector
│   ├── calls the protocol as the adapter with no intermediate custody
│   ├── callbacks cannot mutate capability configuration or reenter manage
│   └── post-borrow health query
│       ├── failures, malformed responses and low health roll back borrowing
│       └── valid health retains funds on the adapter and returns protocol data
├── setMinHealthFactor
│   ├── requires initialization, a self-call and nonzero minimum
│   └── applies the new floor to subsequent borrowing
└── replacement and isolation
    ├── preserves the fixed query, protocol configuration and minimum
    └── adapters sharing an implementation keep independent state
